      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000",
      "widgets_values": [
        "# SAM 3 Video Background Removal (alpha)\n\nRuns fully **locally**: core ComfyUI nodes only, no API nodes, no custom node packs.\nNeeds a recent ComfyUI (one that has the `SAM3_VideoTrack` node). Update ComfyUI if nodes show red.\n\n## Model\nDownload into `ComfyUI/models/checkpoints/`:\n- [sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam3.1/resolve/main/checkpoints/sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors) (1.63 GB)\n\n## How to use\n1. **Load Your Video**.\n2. **What to KEEP**: type the subject, e.g. `person`, `dog`, `woman in red dress`. Several: `person, guitar`. Limit count per prompt with `:N`, e.g. `person:1`. (Max 32 tokens.)\n3. Run. Check **Preview** to see which objects were tracked. To keep only some, put their indices in *Track -> Mask*, e.g. `0` or `0,2`.\n\n## Tuning\n- **detection_threshold**: lower (0.3) if the subject is missed, higher (0.7) if extra things are picked up.\n- **max_objects**: raise for crowds.\n- **Grow/Shrink**: `-1`/`-2` removes a background halo, `+1`/`+2` recovers lost hair/edges.\n- **Softness**: blur_radius 1 = crisp, 3-5 = soft edges.\n\n## Outputs (ComfyUI/output/sam3_bg_removed/)\n- **A. transparent_*.webm**: VP9 with alpha. Plays in browsers, OBS, Premiere/After Effects (with WebM plugin), DaVinci Resolve.\n- **B. png_sequence/frame_*.png**: RGBA PNG per frame. Most reliable for any editor: import as image sequence.\n- **C. alpha_matte_*.mp4**: black/white matte. Use as a track matte / luma key over the original video.\n\nWant ProRes 4444? `ffmpeg -framerate 24 -i frame_%05d_.png -c:v prores_ks -profile:v 4 -pix_fmt yuva444p10le out.mov`"
      ]
    }
